### Vidéo age-restricted (avec cookies JSON exportés)
```bash
# 1. Convertir cookies JSON → Netscape
python3.14 -c "
import json, pathlib
src = pathlib.Path('C:/Users/matth/Downloads/cookies.json')
dst = pathlib.Path('C:/Users/matth/Downloads/cookies_netscape.txt')
data = json.loads(src.read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
cookies = data if isinstance(data, list) else data.get('cookies', [])
lines = ['# Netscape HTTP Cookie File']
for c in cookies:
    domain = c.get('domain',''); flag = 'TRUE' if domain.startswith('.') else 'FALSE'
    path = c.get('path','/'); secure = 'TRUE' if c.get('secure',False) else 'FALSE'
    expiry = int(c.get('expirationDate', c.get('expires',0)) or 0)
    lines.append(f'{domain}\t{flag}\t{path}\t{secure}\t{expiry}\t{c.get(\"name\",\"\")}\t{c.get(\"value\",\"\")}')
dst.write_text('\n'.join(lines), encoding='utf-8')
"
# 2. Télécharger (client web + deno + ejs solver)
python3.14 -m yt_dlp -x --audio-format mp3 --audio-quality 0 \
  --cookies "C:/Users/matth/Downloads/cookies_netscape.txt" \
  --extractor-args "youtube:player_client=web" \
  --js-runtimes "deno:C:/Users/matth/AppData/Local/Microsoft/WinGet/Packages/DenoLand.Deno_Microsoft.Winget.Source_8wekyb3d8bbwe/deno.exe" \
  --remote-components "ejs:github" \
  -o "DOSSIER/%(title)s.%(ext)s" "URL"
```

### Pourquoi `player_client=web` + deno + ejs ?
- YouTube age-restriction → yt-dlp choisit le TV player par défaut avec cookies
- TV player → n-challenge sans n-function → échec
- `player_client=web` force le player web → n-function extractible par deno+EJS solver
- `--remote-components ejs:github` télécharge le solver script depuis GitHub (v0.5.0+)

### Fichiers cookies
- `cookies.json` exporté depuis extension browser (ex: "Get cookies.txt LOCALLY")
- `cookies_netscape.txt` = version convertie (3163 cookies en mars 2026)
